    "result_text": "Done. The full build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added a `capacityWarning` flag to owner responses that is `true` when the owner's city already holds **40\u201349** owners (approaching the hard limit of 50), and `false` otherwise. The hard rejection at 50 (`OwnerCityAtCapacityException`) is untouched.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `capacityWarning` boolean (read-only) property to the `Owner` schema, right after `bulkSignupWarning`, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains a `capacityWarning` getter/setter.\n\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`**:\n   - Added a `CITY_CAPACITY_WARNING_THRESHOLD = 40` constant alongside the existing `CITY_CAPACITY = 50`.\n   - Added `applyCapacityWarning(OwnerDto)`, which counts owners in the owner's city (reusing the same per-city counting as the capacity rejection) and sets the flag when the count is `>= 40 && < 50`.\n   - Called it everywhere `applyBulkSignupWarning` is already called: `getOwner`, `addOwner`, and the idempotent-create replay path \u2014 mirroring the existing warning pattern.\n\nTests: `AcceptanceTest` (including the new `coreWarnsWhenApproachingCapacity`) passes and the full suite is `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
