    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is clean, additive, and idiomatic for this codebase.\n\n- `applyCapacityWarning` is a faithful sibling of the existing `applyBulkSignupWarning`: both are small private helpers that set a single warning flag on the `OwnerDto`, and the three new call sites sit right alongside the existing `applyBulkSignupWarning` calls in the same three response-building spots. A maintainer would find this placement natural.\n- It reuses the existing `countOwnersInCity` helper rather than re-implementing the per-city count, exactly as `applyBulkSignupWarning` reuses `countOwnersRegisteredOn`. The doc even points at `countOwnersInCity` as the shared counting source, so the warning and the hard rejection (`rejectCityAtCapacity`) stay consistent by construction \u2014 no duplicated counting logic.\n- `CITY_CAPACITY_WARNING_THRESHOLD` is declared next to `CITY_CAPACITY` and documented in terms of it, so the 40/50 relationship is expressed as a constant pair rather than a magic number.\n- The OpenAPI `capacityWarning` property mirrors the shape of the neighbouring read-only boolean flags (`bulkSignupWarning`, `possibleDuplicate`).\n\nNo logic is misplaced, nothing is duplicated, and no class or method is becoming a catch-all beyond the warning-helper pattern already established here.",
